 ## Abstract
 
-<!-- p:ABS-01 -->Retrieval in-context captioning places the captions of similar memory images in the prompt of a multimodal model. It needs no training, which suits low-resource languages such as Vietnamese, but a gain over zero-shot prompting may come from seeing any in-domain caption and not from retrieval. This preregistered study, with one look per test set, compares retrieved example captions with an equal number of random captions from the same memory, for two open models, each reported separately. On OpenViIC test, retrieved examples beat random ones by +4.49 [3.52, 5.57] stripped CIDEr-D points pooled (95% bootstrap CI; registered PASS: point above +2.0 and CI above zero). Under the registered scope sentence this gain is "carried mainly by Qwen2.5-VL; not detected for InternVL3". There, the change in count-matched object precision against each model's own zero-shot captions stayed above the registered floor for both models (PASS). On XM3600 Vietnamese, outside the memory's source, the gain was not detected: +0.70 [−0.45, 1.97], a registered FAIL under a rule that required a CI above zero. With the frozen configurations carried to English, the COCO Karpathy test passed (+3.08 [2.08, 4.03] PTB CIDEr-D points; PASS), although InternVL3's reported row there is below zero. On NoCaps the point, +1.73 [0.94, 2.50], lay below the registered +2.0 (FAIL). No transfer claim is made in either language. Crediting a gain to retrieval requires a random-example control at equal k and results per model.
+<!-- p:ABS-01 -->Retrieval in-context captioning places the captions of similar memory images in a multimodal model's prompt. It needs no training, which suits low-resource languages such as Vietnamese, but a gain over zero-shot prompting may come from any in-domain caption, not from retrieval. This preregistered study, with one look per test set, compares retrieved example captions with an equal number of random captions from the same memory, for two open models reported separately. On OpenViIC test, retrieved examples beat random ones by +4.49 [3.52, 5.57] stripped CIDEr-D points pooled (95% bootstrap CI; registered PASS), with the registered scope "carried mainly by Qwen2.5-VL; not detected for InternVL3". There, the change in count-matched object precision against zero-shot stayed above the registered floor for both models (PASS). On XM3600 Vietnamese, outside the memory's source, the gain was not detected: +0.70 [−0.45, 1.97], a registered FAIL under a rule that required a CI above zero. In English, with the frozen configurations, the COCO Karpathy test passed (+3.08 [2.08, 4.03] PTB CIDEr-D points; PASS), although InternVL3's reported row there is below zero. On NoCaps the point, +1.73 [0.94, 2.50], lay below the registered +2.0 (FAIL). No transfer claim is made in either language. Crediting a gain to retrieval requires a random-example control at equal k and results per model.
 
