 <!-- p:S1-03 -->This study measures the first effect against the second. Two open MLLMs caption each image under four prompts: retrieved examples (`ret`), the same number k of random examples from the same memory (`rand`), one fixed example set (`fix`) and zero-shot (`zs`). Configurations were frozen on development data in two registered stages. Each test set was then decoded, scored and decided once, under estimands, thresholds and failure wordings fixed in advance. A separately registered English arm repeated the test with the frozen configurations and no English tuning.
 
