 <!-- p:S3-03 -->**Prompt and decoding.** The prompt follows the image: a fixed Vietnamese header saying that the captions below belong to other images and only show how to write, k numbered example lines, and a tail asking for one short Vietnamese sentence in the examples' style. Tail T1 also asks for only what is visible; tail T2 does not. "Order" places the most similar example first, or last, next to the instruction. The template contains no data-set caption. Decoding is greedy, with at most 60 new tokens, for Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct [@Bai2025Qwen25VL] and InternVL3-8B [@Zhu2025InternVL3].
 
-<!-- p:S3-04 -->**Neighbour-only objects and the deletion step.** An object class is *neighbour-only* when the object matcher finds it in the caption and in at least one shown example, but not in the same model's zero-shot caption. A second model, the verifier, scores each such class as the probability of "yes" to a yes/no question with the image minus that without it; a class scoring below τ is rejected. The caption is split at commas, conjunctions and locative words, and each part naming a rejected class is dropped; if the subject part is hit or the result is malformed, the zero-shot caption is used. At τ = −∞ nothing is rejected.
