 <!-- p:S3-06 -->**Scoring.** Vietnamese candidates and references are lower-cased and segmented into words with RDRSegmenter [@Nguyen2018VnCoreNLP; @Vu2018VnCoreNLP]. CIDEr-D [@Vedantam2015CIDEr] takes its document frequencies from the references of the scored set and is given in points (the score times one hundred). Decisions use *stripped* CIDEr-D, computed after trailing punctuation tokens are dropped from both candidates and references; an arm can then gain nothing from a final period alone.
 
-<!-- p:S3-07 -->**Count-matched object precision** is the instrument of a companion manuscript by the same group (the object-precision study, in preparation), defined here because P2 uses it. For image i, let M_i(run) and M_i(zs) be the distinct object classes matched, in order of first mention, in the run's caption and in the same model's zero-shot caption, and let k_i = min(|M_i(run)|, |M_i(zs)|). tp_cm counts how many of the first k_i classes of the run's caption the gold supports; tp_cm,zs counts the same for the zero-shot caption. Then ΔP_cm = (Σ tp_cm − Σ tp_cm,zs) / Σ k_i, in percentage points. The equal number of mentions keeps a longer caption from being penalised for naming more objects. The gold of an image is the union of the classes that the same manuscript's tone-normalised Vietnamese matcher finds in its references; CHAIR_i [@Rohrbach2018CHAIR] uses the same gold. Verified precision on XM3600 (XM-b) counts all mentions against the released human-verified Open Images labels [@Kuznetsova2020OpenImages].
